{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Math functions",
  "exampleId": "block-functions",
  "description": "The source is 2·sin(πt/2): +2 at 1 s and −2 at 3 s. Read each block at those two instants: the gain of 0.5 gives ±1, |u| gives 2 both times and its square root √2, sign gives ±1, −u gives ∓2, and u² gives 4. The sine and cosine blocks take the clock, so they draw sin t and cos t.",
